.SS "void stumpless_close_network_target (const struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Closes a network target\&. This function closes the network connection associated with the target before destruction\&. It also destroys all memory allocated for the target, including the target struct itself\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this target\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The network target to close\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBbasic_example\&.c\fP, \fBtcp_example\&.c\fP, and \fBudp_example\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "const char * stumpless_get_destination (const struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Gets the destination of a network target\&. The character buffer returned must be freed by the caller when it is no longer needed to avoid memory leaks\&.
.PP
If the network target has been created but not had a destination set yet, the result will be NULL\&.
.PP
In versions prior to v2\&.0\&.0, the returned pointer was to the internal buffer used to store the destination and was not to be modified by the caller\&. This behavior changed in v2\&.0\&.0 in order to avoid thread safety issues\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the target with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the result\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The target to get the destination from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current destination of the network target, or NULL if one has not yet been set\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

