.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_new_network_target (const char * name, enum \fBstumpless_network_protocol\fP network, enum \fBstumpless_transport_protocol\fP transport)"

.PP
Creates a network target, but does not open it\&. A network target can be created with this function if the target needs to be created without initiating a network session\&. This also allows parameters that are not available in the open function to be set before initiating the session, instead of restarting the session on each change\&.
.PP
The target will stay in a paused state until it is opened using the stumpless_open_target function\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the target to open\&. This is only used for identification of the target\&.
.br
\fInetwork\fP The network protocol to use\&.
.br
\fItransport\fP The transport protocol to use\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

